---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Contact & Incident Intake"
	meta_title="Submit Incidents, Confessions & Tips | ErrorLedger"
	description="Submit confidential incident reports, career confessions, or editorial inquiries to The Archivist."
	pubDate={new Date('August 17, 2026')}
	tags={["meta", "contact", "submissions"]}
>
	<h2>The Intake Desk</h2>
	<p>
		ErrorLedger investigates real human, corporate, and systemic failures. If you were involved in a notable disaster, witnessed a bizarre operational blunder, or have access to verifiable public records, we invite your tip.
	</p>

	<h2>Submission Channels</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			<strong>Confidential Incident Inquiries & Tips:</strong><br/>
			<a href="mailto:editor@errorledger.com">editor@errorledger.com</a>
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Anonymous Quick Intake:</strong><br/>
			Use our interactive on-site intake form by clicking <a href="#" data-open-submit-modal><strong>+ Submit an Incident</strong></a> from any page. Submissions are scrubbed of identifying credentials before review.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Factual Corrections & Rights Inquiries:</strong><br/>
			<a href="mailto:corrections@errorledger.com">corrections@errorledger.com</a>
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Whistleblower Protection Standard</h2>
	<p>
		When reviewing Tier 2 submissions, ErrorLedger scrubs names, corporate identifiers, localized database credentials, and internal hostnames unless the incident is already a matter of public legal or regulatory record (Tier 1). We do not disclose confidential sources.
	</p>
</Layout>